Session 36 summary — the zero_silent_loss root-cause chain advanced three proven fixes; the criterion now passes 3-iter runs (2 of 3 attempts), with a new cluster-join failure mode surfacing on the third.

**Fix 1 (build `5B2955EB`, verified):** the sess35 flush→stale retry loop never converged because the stale pass counted `!XBF_DONE` alone as a skip — but that's a block a *prior* pass already staled, still findable via an extra hold. 380 done=0-only skips spun the loop to 79× tries=500 exhaustions and inflated iter walls to 177s. Dropping `!XBF_DONE` from the hazard predicate restored 102-122s walls and eliminated exhaustions.

**Fix 2 (build `1C0589FB`, verified):** both the release-side stale pass and the acquire-side evict pass treated a trylock miss (`-EAGAIN` = cached but locked, e.g. write I/O in flight) identically to not-cached and skipped silently — letting a dir-block image survive on the releasing node's writeback path and clobber peers after unlock (proven by the iter-1 lineage: test4 xfsaild/kworker writes bracketing test3's hold). Now `-EAGAIN` counts as a skip (`P36-STALE-LOCKED`) / blocks gen advance (`P36-EVICT-LOCKED`).

**Fix 3 (build `DE7F1BDA`, the big one, verified):** `mxfs_dlm_reload_inode`'s P34D platter-adoption regressed a node's in-core inode whenever its *own* dinode write was still in flight at a fastex re-acquire. Proven timeline: test10 grew dir nx 22→23 (nlink 1144), its cluster write hadn't landed, the reload adopted the platter's nx=22/nlink=1140 — rolling back the fork and i_size. Consequences: bmbt FUA-read (23 records) vs adopted nx=22 → "corrupt dinode 131 (btree extents)" EUCLEAN mkdir failures; i_size rollback over just-created dirents → the durable silent loss; and the same rollback family produced the iter-3 cluster-wide leaf1-vs-node poisoning that shut down 12 nodes. Fix: skip the reload entirely when the inode's own log item has pending mods (dirty/in-AIL/pinned/ili_fields) — by Invariant 1 no peer can have newer state then. The guard fired 22× during the first passing run.

**Probes added (all always-on under dirwr):** `P36-DINO-WR` uncapped dinode write lineage for low dir inos with nlink, un-ratelimited `P105-REL-DIRINODE` for low inos, nx/nlink in `P-SFDIR-RELOAD`.

**Current state:** build `DE7F1BDA` deployed; 3-iter criterion PASS twice consecutively, then a third run failed differently — iter 3 had 14/16 `join FAIL` (only 2 nodes mounted, mount_s=149, all creates errored). test2 shows `dlm_caw: read_slot I/O error -5` at teardown before the failed rejoin. Note this third run was launched WITHOUT a VM power-cycle (the two passes followed fresh boots) — the join failure may be contaminated-state/SCST stress rather than the dirent-loss bug.

**Next session:** (1) diagnose the iter-3 join-failure mode — check whether it reproduces after a clean power-cycle, examine the form-node's mount output in the harness log and the `read_slot -5` errors; (2) once joins are stable, accumulate more 3-iter passes of zero_silent_loss, then strip/gate the P35x/P36 probes (P35E is un-ratelimited) and proceed down the remaining ship-gate criteria toward a full `verify_ship.sh` run. Criteria not met yet — marker stays unwritten, relay continues.

